License pending

The author is employed by Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory and is
checking how this work must be released under the laboratory's software
release process. Until that check completes, no general license is
granted.

Two narrow permissions stand in the meantime, so the repository's
standing replication experiment stays honest:

1. You may download, install, and run this software to verify the
   records in this repository and to run the replication protocol
   described in REPLICATE.md.
2. GitHub's terms of service govern viewing and forking on the
   platform.

Anything more waits for the review: redistribution outside GitHub,
derivative works, and use of this code inside other projects.

Replication trials remain welcome and do not require a license from us.
The record you produce by running the protocol is yours.

Earlier commits of this repository carried the Apache License 2.0, and
copies obtained under it keep the rights it granted; that history is in
git, not rewritten. This notice governs from this commit forward while
the review is underway. When it concludes, this file will be replaced
by the chosen license.
